// Handles the "View <skill> guide" buttons on the stats (skills) interface.
// Attack, Strength, Defence and Hitpoints share a single combined Combat guide,
// matching how the real 2006 Skill Guides grouped the four core combat stats.
// Every other skill gets its own guide. Content is shown via the existing
// general-purpose book popup (see general/scripts/book.rs2).
//
// Note: each entry below is kept short enough to fit on a single book page.
// proc,book's automatic multi-page split only shows the final page once split,
// so longer text should not be passed to a single ~book(...) call here.

[if_button,stats:com_68]
~book("Combat Guide", "@red@Attack, Strength, Defence & Hitpoints@bla@||Together these four skills make up your combat level, trained through melee fighting.||@red@Attack@bla@ raises your accuracy and which weapons you can wield.|@red@Strength@bla@ raises the damage you deal.|@red@Defence@bla@ reduces incoming hits and unlocks armour.|@red@Hitpoints@bla@ is how much damage you can take before dying, and regenerates over time.");

[if_button,stats:com_69]
~book("Combat Guide", "@red@Attack, Strength, Defence & Hitpoints@bla@||Together these four skills make up your combat level, trained through melee fighting.||@red@Attack@bla@ raises your accuracy and which weapons you can wield.|@red@Strength@bla@ raises the damage you deal.|@red@Defence@bla@ reduces incoming hits and unlocks armour.|@red@Hitpoints@bla@ is how much damage you can take before dying, and regenerates over time.");

[if_button,stats:com_71]
~book("Combat Guide", "@red@Attack, Strength, Defence & Hitpoints@bla@||Together these four skills make up your combat level, trained through melee fighting.||@red@Attack@bla@ raises your accuracy and which weapons you can wield.|@red@Strength@bla@ raises the damage you deal.|@red@Defence@bla@ reduces incoming hits and unlocks armour.|@red@Hitpoints@bla@ is how much damage you can take before dying, and regenerates over time.");

[if_button,stats:com_74]
~book("Combat Guide", "@red@Attack, Strength, Defence & Hitpoints@bla@||Together these four skills make up your combat level, trained through melee fighting.||@red@Attack@bla@ raises your accuracy and which weapons you can wield.|@red@Strength@bla@ raises the damage you deal.|@red@Defence@bla@ reduces incoming hits and unlocks armour.|@red@Hitpoints@bla@ is how much damage you can take before dying, and regenerates over time.");

[if_button,stats:com_70]
~book("Mining Guide", "@red@Mining@bla@||Dig ore, coal and gems out of rock deposits using a pickaxe. A better pickaxe mines faster.||Your level determines which ores you can mine - mithril, adamantite and runite need higher levels.||Smelt ore into bars for Smithing, or sell it for profit. Watch out for rockfalls in the deeper mines.");

[if_button,stats:com_72]
~book("Agility Guide", "@red@Agility@bla@||Improves your stamina - a higher level means run energy drains slower and recovers faster.||Trained mainly on obstacle courses, such as those in the Gnome Stronghold and Barbarian Outpost.||A high level also unlocks handy shortcuts around the world, letting you skip long walks.");

[if_button,stats:com_73]
~book("Smithing Guide", "@red@Smithing@bla@||Smelt ore into bars at a furnace, then hammer bars into weapons and armour on an anvil.||Bronze and iron are available from the start; steel, mithril, adamant and rune need higher levels.||Closely tied to Mining for a steady ore supply - coal is needed alongside ore above iron.");

[if_button,stats:com_75]
~book("Herblore Guide", "@red@Herblore@bla@||Brew potions from herbs and secondary ingredients. Herbs must be cleaned before use.||Combine a clean herb with water in a vial for an unfinished potion, then add the right ingredient.||Potions can restore or boost stats, cure poison, and sell for good profit to other players.");

[if_button,stats:com_76]
~book("Fishing Guide", "@red@Fishing@bla@||Catch fish from rivers, lakes and the sea using nets, bait, rods, harpoons and lobster pots.||Small nets and bait catch shrimp and sardines early; rods and harpoons land trout, tuna and sharks.||Cooking your catch trains Cooking and provides healing food, making Fishing a reliable income source.");

[if_button,stats:com_77]
~book("Ranged Guide", "@red@Ranged@bla@||Attack from a distance using bows and arrows, or crossbows and bolts, instead of fighting up close.||A higher level improves accuracy and unlocks stronger bows and ammunition.||Lighter armour generally works best, since heavy armour can hinder ranged accuracy.");

[if_button,stats:com_78]
~book("Thieving Guide", "@red@Thieving@bla@||Steal from market stalls, pickpocket non-player characters, and open locked chests and doors.||Higher levels reduce your chance of getting caught, and unlock richer targets to steal from.||Getting caught pickpocketing will cause the target to attack you, so be careful at low levels.");

[if_button,stats:com_79]
~book("Cooking Guide", "@red@Cooking@bla@||Prepare raw food, mainly fish and meat, over a fire or on a range to restore Hitpoints when eaten.||Your level determines what you can cook without a high chance of burning it.||Cooking on a range is generally more reliable than an open fire. Cooked food can also be sold.");

[if_button,stats:com_80]
~book("Prayer Guide", "@red@Prayer@bla@||Activate blessings that assist you in combat, at the cost of steadily draining prayer points.||Gain experience by burying bones from defeated monsters, or offering them at a Chaos Altar.||Prayer points restore at an altar or with Prayer potions. Higher levels unlock stronger prayers.");

[if_button,stats:com_81]
~book("Crafting Guide", "@red@Crafting@bla@||Covers working leather, cutting gems, spinning wool, making pottery, and stringing amulets.||Your level determines what you can make, using simple materials like leather, clay and flax.||Higher levels unlock cut gems for jewellery, and dragonhide armour made from dragon hides.");

[if_button,stats:com_82]
~book("Firemaking Guide", "@red@Firemaking@bla@||Light fires using logs and a tinderbox, for light, cooking, and a quick source of experience.||Higher level logs - oak, willow, maple and yew - grant more experience but are harder to light.||Fires burn out after a while and leave ash behind.");

[if_button,stats:com_83]
~book("Magic Guide", "@red@Magic@bla@||Cast spells using runes, from combat spells that damage enemies at range to teleports and enchanting.||Spells are learned automatically as your level rises, and cast from the spellbook interface.||Each spell needs a specific combination of runes, consumed when cast.");

[if_button,stats:com_84]
~book("Fletching Guide", "@red@Fletching@bla@||Create ranged weapons and ammunition - mainly bows and arrows - from logs, strings and feathers.||Cut logs into unstrung bows with a knife, then string them with a bow string to complete them.||Higher levels unlock stronger bows, such as oak, willow, maple and yew.");

[if_button,stats:com_85]
~book("Woodcutting Guide", "@red@Woodcutting@bla@||Chop down trees with an axe to collect logs, used in Firemaking and Fletching, or sold for profit.||A better axe cuts faster. Regular trees are available from the start; oaks, willows, maples and yews need higher levels.||Trees may become stumps after being cut and need time to regrow.");

[if_button,stats:com_240]
~book("Runecrafting Guide", "@red@Runecrafting@bla@||Create your own runes at rune altars scattered across RuneScape, using rune essence.||Visit an altar matching the rune you want, and use essence on it to convert it into runes.||Higher levels let you craft multiple runes from a single piece of essence.");

[if_button,stats:com_244]
~book("Slayer Guide", "@red@Slayer@bla@||Receive tasks from a Slayer Master to hunt down a set number of a particular monster.||Completing a task grants Slayer experience on top of the usual combat rewards.||Some monsters need a high enough Slayer level, or special equipment, to fight safely.");

[if_button,stats:com_266]
~book("Farming Guide", "@red@Farming@bla@||Grow crops - herbs, trees, fruit and vegetables - by planting seeds in patches around RuneScape.||Most patches need weeding before planting, and some crops benefit from protection against disease.||Crops take real time to grow, so check back on your patches to tend and harvest them.");
